" href=\"/en/about\">About</a><a class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium transition-all duration-200 text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card\" href=\"/en/contact\">Contact</a></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"><a class=\"flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card transition-all\" href=\"/ar/courses/ct-mastery/ct-parameters\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-globe w-4 h-4\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"></circle><path d=\"M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20\"></path><path d=\"M2 12h20\"></path></svg><span class=\"hidden sm:inline\">العربية</span></a><button class=\"md:hidden p-2 rounded-lg text-slate-300 hover:text-white hover:bg-brand-card\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu w-5 h-5\"><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"12\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"6\" y2=\"6\"></line><line x1=\"4\" x2=\"20\" y1=\"18\" y2=\"18\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></nav><main class=\"flex-1\"><main dir=\"ltr\" class=\"min-h-screen py-12\"><div class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-slate-400 hover:text-brand-cyan mb-8 transition-colors\" href=\"/en/courses/ct-mastery\"><span>?</span>Back to Course</a><article class=\"bg-brand-card border border-brand-border rounded-2xl p-8\"><div class=\"mb-6\"><span class=\"inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium bg-brand-cyan/10 text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/20\">Lesson</span></div><h1 class=\"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mb-4\">CT Parameters</h1><p class=\"text-slate-400 mb-10\">Duration: <!-- -->22 minutes</p><div class=\"space-y-10\"><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Introduction</h2><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">CT parameters determine how the scanner acquires and reconstructs data. Understanding these parameters is essential for controlling image quality, spatial resolution, image noise, scan speed, and radiation dose. Appropriate parameter selection should always be based on the clinical task and patient characteristics.</p></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Lesson Objectives</h2><div class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\"><div class=\"space-y-2\"><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Explain the main technical parameters used in CT.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Understand the relationship between tube voltage and image quality.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Explain tube current and automatic exposure control.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Understand collimation, slice thickness, and detector configuration.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Explain pitch and its effect on CT acquisition.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Understand rotation time and scan speed.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Recognize the relationship between CT parameters, image noise, and radiation dose.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6\">Lesson Content</h2><div class=\"space-y-8\"><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Overview of CT Parameters</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">CT acquisition depends on several interconnected parameters, including tube voltage, tube current, rotation time, detector configuration, collimation, pitch, and reconstruction settings. Changing one parameter may affect multiple aspects of the examination, so protocol optimization requires understanding their combined effects.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Tube Voltage (kVp)</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Tube voltage determines the energy of the X-ray beam. It influences beam penetration, image contrast, and radiation dose. Lower tube voltage can increase iodine contrast in appropriate examinations, while higher tube voltage provides greater beam penetration for larger patients and dense anatomical regions.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Tube Current (mA)</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Tube current determines the quantity of X-rays produced during acquisition. Increasing tube current generally increases the number of photons reaching the detectors and can reduce image noise, but it also increases radiation exposure. Appropriate tube current should therefore be selected according to patient size and diagnostic requirements.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Tube Current-Time Product (mAs)</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">The tube current-time product represents the amount of tube current applied over a given exposure time. It is an important indicator of the total X-ray output during an acquisition. In general, increasing mAs reduces quantum noise but increases radiation dose.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Automatic Exposure Control</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Automatic exposure control systems adjust tube output according to patient attenuation and examination requirements. These systems can modulate tube current during the scan to maintain an appropriate image quality target while avoiding unnecessary radiation exposure.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Collimation</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Collimation defines the width of the X-ray beam or the detector configuration used for data acquisition. Modern multidetector CT systems use multiple detector rows to acquire a volume of anatomy during each rotation. Appropriate collimation supports efficient scanning and high-quality multiplanar reconstruction.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Slice Thickness</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Slice thickness describes the thickness of the reconstructed image. Thin slices provide improved spatial detail and reduce partial-volume effects but may contain more image noise. Thicker slices generally have lower noise and may be useful for routine review but provide less fine anatomical detail.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Pitch</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Pitch describes the relationship between table movement during one gantry rotation and the total nominal beam width. Pitch influences scan speed, data sampling, image quality, and radiation dose behavior. Its effect depends on the scanner design and the specific acquisition technique.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Rotation Time</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Rotation time is the time required for the gantry to complete one rotation. Shorter rotation times can reduce motion-related artifacts and improve temporal resolution, which is particularly useful in examinations involving rapidly moving anatomy or patients who have difficulty remaining still.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Reconstruction Interval</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Reconstruction interval determines the spacing between reconstructed images. Reconstructions may overlap when thin images are required for multiplanar or three-dimensional processing. The reconstruction interval should be selected according to the clinical purpose and downstream image-processing requirements.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Reconstruction Kernel</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Reconstruction kernels, also called reconstruction algorithms or filters, influence the appearance of CT images. Sharper kernels enhance edge detail and spatial resolution but can increase image noise, while smoother kernels reduce noise and may provide better low-contrast visualization.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Relationship Between Parameters</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">CT parameters should not be considered independently. Tube output, slice thickness, pitch, reconstruction method, and patient size interact to determine image quality and radiation exposure. An optimized protocol balances these factors according to the diagnostic task.</p></div><div class=\"border-l-2 border-brand-cyan/30 pl-5\"><h3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3\">Parameter Selection and Patient Size</h3><p class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\">Patient size strongly influences CT image noise and radiation requirements. Protocols may need adjustment for pediatric patients, small adults, average-sized adults, and larger patients. Patient centering and automatic exposure control can help maintain consistent image quality across different body sizes.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6\">Educational Images</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\"><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/ct-mastery/lesson-03/CT_L03_01_Pitch.jpg\" alt=\"Acquisition Parameters &amp; Techniques - 1\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/ct-mastery/lesson-03/CT_L03_02_Slice_Thickness.jpg\" alt=\"Acquisition Parameters &amp; Techniques - 2\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/ct-mastery/lesson-03/CT_L03_03_Matrix_FOV_Pixel_Size.jpg\" alt=\"Acquisition Parameters &amp; Techniques - 3\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/ct-mastery/lesson-03/CT_L03_04_Digital_Image_Formation.jpg\" alt=\"Acquisition Parameters &amp; Techniques - 4\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><div class=\"overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-slate-900\"><img src=\"/assets/images/en/courses/ct-mastery/lesson-03/CT_L03_05_Rotation_Time.jpg\" alt=\"Acquisition Parameters &amp; Techniques - 5\" class=\"w-full h-auto object-contain\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div></section><section><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4\">Key Points</h2><div class=\"text-slate-300 leading-8\"><div class=\"space-y-2\"><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Tube voltage affects beam energy, tissue contrast, penetration, and radiation dose.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Tube current and mAs influence photon quantity and image noise.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Automatic exposure control adjusts tube output according to patient attenuation.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Collimation and detector configuration determine how CT data are acquired.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Thin slices improve detail but may increase image noise.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Pitch influences table movement, acquisition speed, and dose behavior.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Rotation time affects scan speed and temporal resolution.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->Reconstruction kernels influence the balance between spatial detail and image noise.</p><p>â€¢ <!-- -->CT parameters must be optimized together rather than considered individually.</p></div></div></section></div></article></div></main></main><footer class=\"mt-20 border-t border-brand-border bg-brand-dark\"><div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12\"><div class=\"bg-brand-card border border-brand-border rounded-2xl p-6\"><h3 class=\"text-white font-bold text-lg mb-4 text-center\">Available Payment Methods</h3><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3\"><a href=\"https://wa.me/201115440838\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-4 rounded-xl border transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 border-green-500/20\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-message-circle w-6 h-6\"><path d=\"M7.9 20A9 9 0 1 0 4 16.1L2 22Z\"></path></svg><span class=\"text-sm font-medium\">WhatsApp</span><span class=\"text-xs opacity-70\">01115440838</span></a><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-4 rounded-xl border transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 bg-red-500/10 text-red-400 border-red-500/20\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-smartphone w-6 h-6\"><rect width=\"14\" height=\"20\" x=\"5\" y=\"2\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M12 18h.01\"></path></svg><span class=\"text-sm font-medium\">Vodafone Cash</span><span class=\"text-xs opacity-70\">01002293344</span></a><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-4 rounded-xl border transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105 bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 border-blue-500/20\"><svg 